[Music]  [Applause]  hi I'm Evan Carmichael  welcome to the edition of ask Evan today  I'm going to answer a question from one  of our forum readers wrote in asking  about fundraising so the question is how  everyone I'm looking for fundraising  ideas for nonprofits I know I can learn  a lot thanks for the question  to quickly answer it for you and I've  been on boards of nonprofit and charity  organizations in the past it can be  really tough you know everybody's asking  for donations and you have to separate  yourself from everybody else so I don't  know what what your nonprofit is doing  but you have to really find a way to  tell your story and a lot of the times  the people who are in charity work and  nonprofit are not great marketers and  they're not great at telling their  stories and the ones who raise the most  money are the ones who do a good job of  telling their story so I don't how much  money you're trying to raise or again  what it is that you do but you have to  create an emotional connection with  people who can potentially give you  money so what are you trying to raise  the money for and how can you tie that  home to a personal story of somebody and  draw me in and make me want to care  about this right we're bombarded all day  with tons of different messages and so  to make somebody stop and take 10  minutes out of their day to watch a  video or to go to your website and read  your story it's got to be compelling  right so don't just say what you do  explain how you do it and show the  people who you're helping so you know  smiling people how their testimonials  explain the importance of what it is  that you're doing so that's number one  for any marketing that you do for any  awareness if somebody's hitting your  website they see a brochure they see a  flyer it's got to have a strong  emotional immediate impact with the  person to make them care and want to at  least find out a little bit more about  what you're doing number one the second  thing is I try to get people involved in  the organization who have some  connection so when I was on the board of  Junior Achievement part of what we did  was raise funds through our own  connections so you're bringing up  people who can help not just with their  volunteer time but can also help raise  money either personally or through their  friends so often they'll have events if  it's a dinner or golf tournament or  something fun where you can try to get  corporate sponsors but also the people  who are involved try to line up their  own you know sponsors or their own  connections to be able to buy some of  the spots so you want to try to create a  board of advisers or Board of Directors  who can also not just give you advice  and can work hard and be volunteers but  can also provide you with financial  support and connections to financial  support so the most successful charities  and nonprofits again are the ones who  have a good board of advisers or  directors who are actively involved  committing their time but also  committing their dollars and getting  their friends involved as well so along  with telling your story and along with  getting the people involved the last  thing I would think of is really have a  clear vision for what you want to  accomplish so what is it that you're  trying to do and how does the world  gonna be better because of it right so  as much as possible you want to tie  people into that vision and get them  excited about the new world that you're  going to be able to create if they help  you with ABC right so there are that  many visions that are easy to get  excited about right and again people are  bombarded with messaging so if you give  them something that genuinely they can  get excited about and and you know be  really happy about then they are more  likely to get involved with you so what  is the world that you want to create and  it might be a massive vision I don't  know what the nonprofit again is about  it could be a local community vision  it's fine as long as you have a clear  vision for what you want to do number of  people help something you want to build  all the benefits attached to that the  more you have a clearly defined vision  that gets people excited the easier is  going to be they get people to come on  board and help them so hopefully those  ideas helped you if you like the video  please give it a thumbs up but makes  gonna do more for you and if you have a  question about this video you have a  comment  or question about your own business I'd  love to hear from you if you want to  leave it in the comment section below I  always read those I appreciate them and  I really like seeing them come in so  thank you and you'll see you on the next  episode  [Music]  you  [Music]

